<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pt-16 pb-14 sm:pt-24" aria-labelledby="home-title">
  <div class="grid lg:grid-cols-[1.1fr_1fr] gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-center">
    <div>
      <.eyebrow label="An API for agents with things to do" align={:left} />
      <h1 id="home-title" class="mt-6 text-5xl sm:text-6xl leading-[1.02] tracking-tight">
        Big ideas.<br />Small goat.<br />
        <span class="text-[var(--color-brand)]">Real computers.</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-7 text-lg leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] max-w-lg">
        Managoat is open-source infrastructure for running agents through an API.
        Give Claude Code, Codex or Gemini CLI a sandbox, files and tools.
        Build whatever delightful thing you had in mind on top.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center">
        <a
          href="/docs/quickstart"
          class="inline-flex px-5 py-3 bg-[var(--color-brand)] text-white font-medium rounded-md hover:bg-[var(--color-brand-hover)]"
        >
          Make your first API call →
        </a>
        <a
          href="/docs/self-hosting"
          class="text-sm underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-brand)]"
        >
          Run your own instance
        </a>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Self-hosted. Apache-2.0. Mildly goat-themed.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure class="relative border border-[var(--color-border-strong)] bg-[var(--color-bg-1)] p-6 sm:p-8 lg:rotate-2">
      <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-4">
        <span class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest">Field notes / 001</span>
        <span class="text-xs italic text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">The useful bit underneath</span>
      </figcaption>
      <div class="py-7 text-center">
        <p class="text-2xl font-semibold" style="font-family: var(--paper-display)">
          Your wonderfully specific app
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          A button. A chat. A cron job. Your call.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-3 text-[var(--color-brand)]" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="flex-1 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--color-border-strong)]"></span>
        <span class="font-mono text-xs">↓ HTTP / SDK ↑ events + results</span>
        <span class="flex-1 border-t border-dashed border-[var(--color-border-strong)]"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="my-6 flex gap-5 items-center">
        <img
          src={Site.Brand.asset("mark-mono.png")}
          alt=""
          width="64"
          height="64"
          data-role="brand-mark"
          class="h-16 shrink-0"
        />
        <div>
          <p class="text-2xl font-semibold" style="font-family: var(--paper-display)">Managoat</p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
            Starts the machine. Runs the agent.<br />Keeps track of the conversation.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="border border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-2)] p-5">
        <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          One conversation’s sandbox
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-sm">A coding agent + a real filesystem + a shell</p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          Your repositories, packages, skills and tools.
        </p>
      </div>
      <p class="mt-5 text-right text-sm italic text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Goat for scale. Computer for work.
      </p>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-14" aria-labelledby="possibilities-title">
  <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border-strong)] pt-12">
    <.eyebrow label="A few things we’ve built" align={:left} />
    <div class="mt-4 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 items-end">
      <h2 id="possibilities-title" class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl leading-tight">
        The API is plumbing.<br />The possibilities are the point.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Here are a few things we’ve built on it. Real apps, open source, with different ideas
        about what an agent ought to feel like. Borrow liberally.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-10 grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-x-10">
      <article
        :for={{app, index} <- Enum.with_index(homepage_apps(), 1)}
        class="border-t border-[var(--color-border)] py-7"
      >
        <div class="flex gap-4 items-baseline">
          <span class="font-mono text-xs text-[var(--color-brand)]">{String.pad_leading(
            to_string(index),
            2,
            "0"
          )}</span>
          <h3 class="text-2xl">{app.name}</h3>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">{app.blurb}</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          <span class="font-medium text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">Under the hood:</span> {app.shows}.
        </p>
        <a
          href={app.source}
          class="inline-block mt-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-brand)] underline underline-offset-4"
        >See how it’s built →</a>
      </article>
    </div>
    <a
      href="/built-with"
      class="inline-block mt-3 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-brand)] underline underline-offset-4"
    >Visit the whole menagerie →</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section
  class="bg-[var(--color-band)] border-y border-[var(--color-border)]"
  aria-labelledby="workbench-title"
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-14 grid lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] gap-10 items-center">
    <div>
      <.eyebrow label="Exhibit A" align={:left} />
      <h2 id="workbench-title" class="mt-4 text-3xl sm:text-4xl leading-tight">
        A little workshop<br />for a lot of work.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Workbench turns projects, tasks and agents into a place to get things done.
        Assign a task, follow the work, and pick up the conversation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Its interface is an app built on Managoat’s public API. The same building blocks
        are there for your own workshop, research desk, or odd little weekend project.
      </p>
      <a
        href={homepage_workbench().source}
        class="inline-block mt-6 text-sm font-medium text-[var(--color-brand)] underline underline-offset-4"
      >Peek inside Workbench →</a>
    </div>
    <figure class="min-w-0">
      <a
        href={homepage_workbench().screenshot.src}
        aria-label="View the Workbench screenshot at full size"
      >
        <img
          src={homepage_workbench().screenshot.src}
          alt={homepage_workbench().screenshot.alt}
          width="973"
          height="791"
          loading="lazy"
          class="w-full border border-[var(--color-border-strong)]"
        />
      </a>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Workbench, with a seeded local example. One possible shape for the API.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 py-16" aria-labelledby="api-title">
  <.eyebrow label="Yes, there is an API under the goat" align={:left} />
  <div class="mt-5 grid lg:grid-cols-2 gap-10">
    <div>
      <h2 id="api-title" class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl leading-tight">
        Send a task.<br />Get some actual work back.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Your app sends the prompt. Managoat provisions a sandbox and runs the agent.
        Stream its progress, read the result, and send a follow-up to the conversation.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
        Configure reusable agents and environments, connect MCP tools, and provide credentials
        for the job. Managoat handles the machines and their lifecycle.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm text-[var(--color-brand)]">
        <a href="/docs/quickstart" class="underline underline-offset-4">First API request →</a>
        <a href="/docs/primitives" class="underline underline-offset-4">The four building blocks →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="min-w-0 border border-[var(--color-border-strong)]">
      <div class="flex justify-between px-5 py-3 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] bg-[var(--color-bg-1)] text-xs font-mono">
        <span>hello-goat.ts</span><span class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">@managoat/sdk</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="p-5 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-7 bg-[var(--color-code-bg)] text-[var(--color-code-text)]"><code>{homepage_example()}</code></pre>
      <p class="px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        After creating an agent, set MANAGOAT_BASE_URL and MANAGOAT_API_KEY in your server’s environment.
        Replace the example agent ID with yours.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16" aria-labelledby="timing-title">
  <div class="border-t border-[var(--color-border-strong)] pt-12">
    <.eyebrow label="Go from idea to running agent" align={:left} />
    <div class="mt-5 grid lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] gap-10">
      <div>
        <h2 id="timing-title" class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl leading-tight">
          A fresh sandbox.<br />In seconds.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-5 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          Send a prompt and Managoat gets a computer ready for the job.
          In this snapshot, median sandbox provisioning and setup took
          <strong class="text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">4.7–5.0 seconds for Claude Code</strong>
          and <strong class="text-[var(--color-text-primary)]">9.2–9.8 seconds for Codex</strong>,
          across the two providers.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] leading-relaxed">
          Then the runtime starts and the agent gets to work. The first-text column
          includes that whole path from the prompt arriving at Managoat.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          A snapshot from our instance’s Tempo traces, 15–16 October 2026. {homepage_benchmark()[
            "complete_phase_samples"
          ]} cold starts with complete phase timings,
          drawn from {homepage_benchmark()["matched_cold_turns"]} traced cold turns.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="min-w-0">
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
            <caption class="sr-only">
              Median cold-start timings by runtime and sandbox provider
            </caption>
            <thead class="border-b border-[var(--color-border-strong)]">
              <tr>
                <th scope="col" class="py-3 pr-3 font-medium">Runtime / sandbox</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-3 px-2 font-medium text-right">Sandbox + setup</th>
                <th scope="col" class="py-3 pl-2 font-medium text-right">Prompt → first text</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr
                :for={row <- homepage_benchmark()["results"]}
                class="border-b border-[var(--color-border)]"
              >
                <th scope="row" class="py-4 pr-3 font-normal">
                  <span class="block">{row["runtime"]} / {row["provider"]}</span>
                  <span class="block mt-1 text-xs text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">{row[
                    "samples"
                  ]} samples</span>
                </th>
                <td class="py-4 px-2 text-right font-mono text-[var(--color-brand)]">
                  {seconds(row["sandbox_setup_median_seconds"])}
                </td>
                <td class="py-4 pl-2 text-right font-mono">
                  {seconds(row["first_text_median_seconds"])}
                </td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          Medians of traced requests that reached first text and had every phase recorded.
          Failed launches and incomplete timings are excluded; this is not a success-rate claim.
          Models and workloads vary, and the Sprites/Codex sample is small.
          Times exclude client transport and rendering.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-4 text-sm text-[var(--color-brand)]">
          <a
            href="/site/benchmarks/cold-starts-2026-10-16.json"
            class="underline underline-offset-4"
          >Snapshot and method (JSON) →</a>
          <a href="/docs/guides/operate/observability" class="underline underline-offset-4">How we measure it →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 pb-16" aria-labelledby="start-title">
  <div class="border-y border-[var(--color-border-strong)] py-10 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-8">
    <div>
      <p class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
        Some assembly encouraged
      </p>
      <h2 id="start-title" class="mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-4xl">Bring your own bright idea.</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[var(--color-text-secondary)] max-w-xl">
        Run Managoat on your infrastructure, bring your model credentials, and make it yours.
        This site is the maintainer’s own instance.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="shrink-0 flex flex-col items-start gap-4">
      <a
        href="/docs/self-hosting"
        class="px-5 py-3 bg-[var(--color-brand)] text-white rounded-md font-medium hover:bg-[var(--color-brand-hover)]"
      >Set up your instance →</a>
      <a
        href="/dashboard"
        class="text-sm underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-[var(--color-brand)]"
      >Already have an account? Dashboard →</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
